{"base_rate":0.40290620871862615,"brier":0.1874784676354029,"bss":0.22069963441172202,"bss_hi":0.3193771049370109,"bss_lo":0.11229774714576927,"chart":{"base":[584.4,172.0],"fp":[301.7,216.8],"lead":"62,278.3 272,248.3 482,210.4 692,157.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.22 — higher than 22% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +22pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 93% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 13%; promised 94% → rained 73%"},"rel":"83.4,410.4 325.7,337.6 653.9,152.6"},"country":"FI","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.15141347424042273,"ess":377.0942853719904,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Helsinki</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Helsinki rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nHELSINKI KAISANIEMI AWS, 0.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.22, ranked 105 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(65&ndash;118) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>233</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Helsinki</b> <span class=\"muted\">FI</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.22</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>65&ndash;118\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Helsinki &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Helsinki\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=